@startuml
title COLORS Web Application — Class / Module Diagram
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
class "ColorsUI (js/code.js)" <<JavaScript module>> {
  - userId : number
  - firstName : string
  - lastName : string
  + doLogin()
  + saveCookie()
  + readCookie()
  + doLogout()
  + addColor()
  + searchColor()
}
class "Login.php" <<PHP endpoint>> {
  + POST(login, password)
  + returnWithInfo(firstName, lastName, id)
  + returnWithError(error)
}
class "AddColor.php" <<PHP endpoint>> {
  + POST(color, userId)
}
class "SearchColors.php" <<PHP endpoint>> {
  + POST(search, userId)
}
class "Users" <<database table>> {
  + ID
  + Login
  + Password
  + firstName
  + lastName
}
class "Colors" <<database table>> {
  + UserId
  + Name
}
ColorsUI ..> "Login.php" : XMLHttpRequest (JSON)
ColorsUI ..> "AddColor.php" : XMLHttpRequest (JSON)
ColorsUI ..> "SearchColors.php" : XMLHttpRequest (JSON)
"Login.php" ..> Users : SELECT credentials
"AddColor.php" ..> Colors : INSERT color
"SearchColors.php" ..> Colors : SELECT matching colors
Users "1" -- "0..*" Colors : owner (UserId)
note bottom of ColorsUI
  Browser code is procedural: these are module functions,
  not declared JavaScript classes. The SQL tables are
  inferred from queries; full schema is not in repository.
end note
@enduml
